{"id": "EUVD-2026-81769", "enisaUuid": "7bb7f454-8a36-3a44-ac8f-b60c9182f857", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: Do not skip lock checks for single-byte ranges\n\ncheck_lock_range() uses inclusive ranges. Its callers pass the end\noffset as start + length - 1, so start == end represents a valid\nsingle-byte range rather than an empty range.\n\nThe start == end shortcut therefore skips mandatory byte-range lock\nchecks for one-byte reads, writes, copychunk operations and one-byte\ntruncate ranges. A conflicting lock covering that byte is not checked\nand the operation is allowed to proceed.\n\nRemove the shortcut. The truncate size == inode->i_size case is already\nhandled by only calling check_lock_range() when the new size differs\nfrom the current file size.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:13", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a89cc145832e81c32199d4ca2e1ea8bd51ed601d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/993e0158331d37c04da18efe551b5e1e35fb3078", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f751d6e39d4c937c45f8fedc66699aa7d2d52288", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84c2d8e807ac489f5c91769293fb15dfdae8bae8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07a9e289ff7edcc004f58952405f8a65c4e37512", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d40c24634fe077a0dc91fd11fccf44ce12b454d5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rxgv-prwv-26g4", "CVE-2026-90176"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "29eb2938-22bc-362f-acbb-e9874ad67991", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "2db0125d-b7f6-3049-b287-afdef7913ac3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.120 <6.6.157"}, {"id": "2fc41a89-43cc-3e8c-a9d8-e12ee6aa5ee4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "pro